_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 11
---
order: 11
---
short_label: XII.11
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Cones and cylinders of the same height are to one another as their bases.
----
proof:

Let there be cones and cylinders of the same height, let the circles {ABCD|circABCD} and {EFGH|circEFGH} be their bases, {KL} and {MN} their axes, and {AC} and {EG} the diameters of their bases.

I say that the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as the cone {AL|coneAL} is to the cone {EN|coneEN}.

<center>
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="560" height="300" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XII.11 diagram" src="propXII11.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // XII.2's double reductio carried up to cones. Case 1: O less than the
    // cone EN, X the difference. The square, then the octagon, inscribed in
    // EFGH carry pyramids taking more than half of what is left of the cone
    // each time (XII.6, X.1), until the pyramid on HPEQFRGS exceeds O; the
    // similar pyramid in AL then gives, through XII.1, XII.2, XII.6, V.11 and
    // V.16, O greater than it too — impossible. Case 2 inverts to case 1.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws the two circles, the squares and octagons in
    // them, the diameters AC, EG, the axes KL, MN, and the solids O and X;
    // the cones themselves are not drawn. All kept. The square EFGH, the
    // octagon EQFRGSHP, and the square and octagon in ABCD are held back
    // until the proof inscribes them, and O and X until it posits them.
    // Everything added is transparent: faceless twins of the circles,
    // squares and octagons (circABCD, circEFGH, sqEFGH, DTAUBVCW, HPEQFRGS —
    // the originals have opaque faces, raised over the figure when lit,
    // #140); the cones' axial triangles (coneAL, coneEN), which stand for
    // the cones in the prose; the arcs, chords and triangles on EFGH; the
    // square circumscribed about EFGH (circSq, corners E+F less M, ...);
    // the pyramids' apex edges from N and L; and the twelve edges of O and
    // X (a polyhedron draws no highlight), built as on XII.5: Of / Xf, an
    // octagon walking the outline (the target of the prose refs), and five
    // lines each. The cylinders are not drawn; their slides light the bases
    // and axes.
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, C, E, G, L lineSliders,
    // givens; A0, A3, L3 off-canvas; O0..O3 and X0..X3 free, the handles of
    // O and X, deferred so the solids follow `visible`. B, D, F, H, K, M, N
    // and P..W are derived and listed per slide. Resting figure unaffected.
    var GIVEN = ["Kcirc","Mcirc","circABCD","circEFGH","coneAL","coneEN",
                 "A","B","C","D","K","E","F","G","H","M","AC","EG",
                 "L","N","KL","MN"];
    var OBOX  = ["Of","Odc","Odd","Obb","Oba","Obc"];
    var XBOX  = ["Xf","Xdc","Xdd","Xbb","Xba","Xbc"];
    var OSET  = ["O","O0","O1","O2","O3","Oc","Ob2","Od2","Oc2"].concat(OBOX);
    var XSET  = ["X","X0","X1","X2","X3","Xc","Xb2","Xd2","Xc2"].concat(XBOX);
    var SO    = GIVEN.concat(OSET);
    var SOX   = SO.concat(XSET);
    var SQ    = SOX.concat(["EFGH","sqEFGH"]);
    var NSQ   = ["nE","nF","nG","nH"];
    var NOCT  = ["nP","nQ","nR","nS"];
    var NZ    = ["nZ1","nZ2","nZ3","nZ4"];
    var LOCT  = ["lD","lT","lA","lU","lB","lV","lC","lW"];
    var PSQ   = SQ.concat(NSQ);
    var CSQ   = PSQ.concat(["circSq"]);
    var PCS   = CSQ.concat(NZ);
    var BIS   = SQ.concat(["P","Q","R","S"]);
    var CHORDS = ["HP","PE","EQ","QF","FR","RG","GS","SH"];
    var ARCS  = ["arcEF","arcFG","arcGH","arcHE"];
    var TRIS  = ["HPE","EQF","FRG","GSH"];
    var OCT   = BIS.concat(["EQFRGSHP","HPEQFRGS"]);
    var TRI   = OCT.concat(TRIS);
    var PYT   = TRI.concat(NSQ).concat(NOCT);
    var PYO   = OCT.concat(NSQ).concat(NOCT);
    var POLY2 = PYO.concat(["T","U","V","W","ABCD","AUBVCWDT","DTAUBVCW"]);
    var PYL   = POLY2.concat(LOCT);
    var CONE_AL = ["circABCD","coneAL"];
    var CONE_EN = ["circEFGH","coneEN"];
    var CIRCS = ["circABCD","circEFGH"];
    var PYR_SQ = ["sqEFGH","N"].concat(NSQ);
    var PYR_CS = ["circSq","N"].concat(NZ);
    var PYR_N = ["HPEQFRGS","N"].concat(NSQ).concat(NOCT);
    var PYR_L = ["DTAUBVCW","L"].concat(LOCT);
    var REST  = GIVEN.concat(OSET).concat(XSET).concat(["EFGH","P","Q","R",
                 "S","EQFRGSHP","T","U","V","W","ABCD","AUBVCWDT"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "XII.11",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,160;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,160;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,40,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,210,0",
            "K;point;midpoint;A,C",
            "Kcirc;circle;radius;K,A;0;0;black;random",
            "B;point;perpendicular;K,A",
            "D;point;extend;B,K,K,A",
            "U';point;midpoint;A,B;0;0",
            "U;point;cutoff;K,U',K,A",
            "V';point;midpoint;B,C;0;0",
            "V;point;cutoff;K,V',K,A",
            "W';point;midpoint;C,D;0;0",
            "W;point;cutoff;K,W',K,A",
            "T';point;midpoint;D,A;0;0",
            "T;point;cutoff;K,T',K,A",
            "AUBVCWDT;polygon;octagon;A,U,B,V,C,W,D,T;0;0;black;random",
            "ABCD;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,C,D;0;0;black;random",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "E;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,260,0",
            "G;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,390,0",
            "M;point;midpoint;E,G",
            "Mcirc;circle;radius;M,E;0;0;black;random",
            "F;point;perpendicular;M,E",
            "H;point;extend;F,M,M,E",
            "Q';point;midpoint;E,F;0;0",
            "Q;point;cutoff;M,Q',M,E",
            "R';point;midpoint;F,G;0;0",
            "R;point;cutoff;M,R',M,E",
            "S';point;midpoint;G,H;0;0",
            "S;point;cutoff;M,S',M,E",
            "P';point;midpoint;H,E;0;0",
            "P;point;cutoff;M,P',M,E",
            "EQFRGSHP;polygon;octagon;E,Q,F,R,G,S,H,P;0;0;black;random",
            "EFGH;polygon;quadrilateral;E,F,G,H;0;0;black;random",
            "EG;line;connect;E,G",
            "L3;point;free;2000,-10000;0;0",
            "L;point;lineSlider;K,L3,130,40",
            "KL;line;connect;K,L",
            "N;point;cutoff;M,L3,K,L",
            "MN;line;connect;M,N",
            "O0;point;free;440,240;0;0",
            "O1;point;free;440,160;0;0",
            "O2;point;free;480,210;0;0",
            "O3;point;free;510,240;0;0",
            "O;polyhedron;parallelepiped;O0,O1,O2,O3;black;0;black;random",
            "X0;point;free;480,100;0;0",
            "X1;point;free;480,60;0;0",
            "X2;point;free;500,80;0;0",
            "X3;point;free;530,100;0;0",
            "X;polyhedron;parallelepiped;X0,X1,X2,X3;black;0;black;random",
            // Faceless twins of the circles, squares and octagons (see above).
            "circABCD;circle;radius;K,A;0;0;0;0",
            "circEFGH;circle;radius;M,E;0;0;0;0",
            "sqEFGH;polygon;quadrilateral;E,F,G,H;0;0;0;0",
            "DTAUBVCW;polygon;octagon;D,T,A,U,B,V,C,W;0;0;0;0",
            "HPEQFRGS;polygon;octagon;H,P,E,Q,F,R,G,S;0;0;0;0",
            // The cones' axial triangles, standing for the cones AL and EN.
            "coneAL;polygon;triangle;A,L,C;0;0;0;0",
            "coneEN;polygon;triangle;E,N,G;0;0;0;0",
            // The chords, the circumferences bisected, and the triangles.
            "HP;line;connect;H,P;0;0;0",
            "PE;line;connect;P,E;0;0;0",
            "EQ;line;connect;E,Q;0;0;0",
            "QF;line;connect;Q,F;0;0;0",
            "FR;line;connect;F,R;0;0;0",
            "RG;line;connect;R,G;0;0;0",
            "GS;line;connect;G,S;0;0;0",
            "SH;line;connect;S,H;0;0;0",
            "arcEF;sector;arc;E,Q,F;0;0;0;0",
            "arcFG;sector;arc;F,R,G;0;0;0;0",
            "arcGH;sector;arc;G,S,H;0;0;0;0",
            "arcHE;sector;arc;H,P,E;0;0;0;0",
            "HPE;polygon;triangle;H,P,E;0;0;0;0",
            "EQF;polygon;triangle;E,Q,F;0;0;0;0",
            "FRG;polygon;triangle;F,R,G;0;0;0;0",
            "GSH;polygon;triangle;G,S,H;0;0;0;0",
            // The square circumscribed about EFGH.
            "Z1;point;parallelogram;E,M,F;0;0",
            "Z2;point;parallelogram;F,M,G;0;0",
            "Z3;point;parallelogram;G,M,H;0;0",
            "Z4;point;parallelogram;H,M,E;0;0",
            "circSq;polygon;quadrilateral;Z1,Z2,Z3,Z4;0;0;0;0",
            // Apex edges of the pyramids set up in the cones.
            "nE;line;connect;N,E;0;0;0",
            "nF;line;connect;N,F;0;0;0",
            "nG;line;connect;N,G;0;0;0",
            "nH;line;connect;N,H;0;0;0",
            "nP;line;connect;N,P;0;0;0",
            "nQ;line;connect;N,Q;0;0;0",
            "nR;line;connect;N,R;0;0;0",
            "nS;line;connect;N,S;0;0;0",
            "nZ1;line;connect;N,Z1;0;0;0",
            "nZ2;line;connect;N,Z2;0;0;0",
            "nZ3;line;connect;N,Z3;0;0;0",
            "nZ4;line;connect;N,Z4;0;0;0",
            "lD;line;connect;L,D;0;0;0",
            "lT;line;connect;L,T;0;0;0",
            "lA;line;connect;L,A;0;0;0",
            "lU;line;connect;L,U;0;0;0",
            "lB;line;connect;L,B;0;0;0",
            "lV;line;connect;L,V;0;0;0",
            "lC;line;connect;L,C;0;0;0",
            "lW;line;connect;L,W;0;0;0",
            // The other four corners of O and of X, then their twelve edges.
            "Oc;point;parallelogram;O1,O0,O2;0;0",
            "Ob2;point;parallelogram;O1,O0,O3;0;0",
            "Od2;point;parallelogram;O2,O0,O3;0;0",
            "Oc2;point;parallelogram;Oc,O0,O3;0;0",
            "Of;polygon;octagon;O0,O1,Oc,Oc2,Od2,O3,O0,O2;0;0;0;0",
            "Odc;line;connect;O2,Oc;0;0;0",
            "Odd;line;connect;O2,Od2;0;0;0",
            "Obb;line;connect;O1,Ob2;0;0;0",
            "Oba;line;connect;Ob2,O3;0;0;0",
            "Obc;line;connect;Ob2,Oc2;0;0;0",
            "Xc;point;parallelogram;X1,X0,X2;0;0",
            "Xb2;point;parallelogram;X1,X0,X3;0;0",
            "Xd2;point;parallelogram;X2,X0,X3;0;0",
            "Xc2;point;parallelogram;Xc,X0,X3;0;0",
            "Xf;polygon;octagon;X0,X1,Xc,Xc2,Xd2,X3,X0,X2;0;0;0;0",
            "Xdc;line;connect;X2,Xc;0;0;0",
            "Xdd;line;connect;X2,Xd2;0;0;0",
            "Xbb;line;connect;X1,Xb2;0;0;0",
            "Xba;line;connect;Xb2,X3;0;0;0",
            "Xbc;line;connect;Xb2,Xc2;0;0;0"
        ],
        deferDraggables: ["O0","O1","O2","O3","X0","X1","X2","X3"],
        slides: [
            { text: "“Cones and cylinders of the same height are to one another as their bases.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(CONE_EN),
              justifications: [{ ref: "XII.11" }] },
            { text: "Let there be cones and cylinders of the same height,",
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(CONE_EN).concat(["KL","MN"]) },
            { text: "let the circles {ABCD|circABCD} and {EFGH|circEFGH} be their bases, {KL} and {MN} their axes,",
              highlighted: CIRCS.concat(["KL","MN"]) },
            { text: "and {AC} and {EG} the diameters of their bases.",
              highlighted: ["AC","EG"] },
            { text: "I say that the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH}",
              highlighted: CIRCS },
            { text: "as the cone {AL|coneAL} is to the cone {EN|coneEN}.",
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(CONE_EN) },
            { text: "For, if not, then the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as the cone {AL|coneAL} is",
              highlighted: CIRCS.concat(["coneAL"]) },
            { text: "either to some solid less than the cone {EN|coneEN} or to a greater.",
              highlighted: CONE_EN },
            { text: "First, let it be in that ratio to a less solid {O|Of},",
              visible: SO,
              highlighted: OBOX },
            { text: "and let the solid {X|Xf} be equal to that by which the solid {O|Of} is less than the cone {EN|coneEN}.",
              visible: SOX,
              highlighted: XBOX.concat(OBOX).concat(CONE_EN) },
            { text: "Therefore the cone {EN|coneEN} equals the sum of the solids {O|Of} and {X|Xf}.",
              highlighted: CONE_EN.concat(OBOX).concat(XBOX) },
            { text: "Inscribe the square {EFGH|sqEFGH} in the circle {EFGH|circEFGH}.",
              visible: SQ,
              highlighted: ["sqEFGH"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "EFGH", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "square inscribed in a circle", ref: "IV.6" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the square is greater than the half of the circle.",
              highlighted: ["sqEFGH","circEFGH"] },
            { text: "Set up from the square {EFGH|sqEFGH} a pyramid of equal height with the cone.",
              visible: PSQ,
              highlighted: PYR_SQ,
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "nE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "nF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "nG", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "nH", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore the pyramid so set up is greater than the half of the cone,",
              highlighted: PYR_SQ.concat(CONE_EN) },
            { text: "for if we circumscribe a square about the circle,",
              visible: CSQ,
              highlighted: ["circSq","circEFGH"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "circSq", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "and set up from it a pyramid of equal height with the cone,",
              visible: PCS,
              highlighted: PYR_CS,
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "nZ1", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "nZ2", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "nZ3", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "nZ4", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "then the inscribed pyramid is half of the circumscribed pyramid,",
              highlighted: PYR_SQ.concat(PYR_CS) },
            { text: "for they are to one another as their bases,",
              highlighted: ["sqEFGH","circSq"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "pyramids of the same height as their bases", ref: "XII.6" }] },
            { text: "while the cone is less than the circumscribed pyramid.",
              highlighted: CONE_EN.concat(PYR_CS) },
            { text: "Bisect the circumferences {EF|arcEF}, {FG|arcFG}, {GH|arcGH}, and {HE|arcHE} at the points {P}, {Q}, {R}, and {S},",
              visible: BIS,
              highlighted: ARCS.concat(["P","Q","R","S"]),
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "P", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "Q", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "R", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "S", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "and join {HP}, {PE}, {EQ}, {QF}, {FR}, {RG}, {GS}, and {SH}.",
              visible: OCT,
              highlighted: CHORDS,
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "EQFRGSHP", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore each of the triangles {HPE}, {EQF}, {FRG}, and {GSH}",
              visible: TRI,
              highlighted: TRIS },
            { text: "is greater than the half of that segment of the circle about it.",
              highlighted: TRIS.concat(ARCS) },
            { text: "Set up on each of the triangles {HPE}, {EQF}, {FRG}, and {GSH} a pyramid of equal height with the cone.",
              visible: PYT,
              highlighted: TRIS.concat(NOCT).concat(["N"]),
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "nP", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "nQ", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "nR", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "nS", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore each of the pyramids so set up",
              highlighted: TRIS.concat(NSQ).concat(NOCT) },
            { text: "is also greater than the half of that segment of the cone about it.",
              highlighted: TRIS.concat(NSQ).concat(NOCT).concat(ARCS) },
            { text: "Thus, bisecting the circumferences which are left, joining straight lines,",
              visible: PYO,
              highlighted: ["HPEQFRGS"] },
            { text: "setting up on each of the triangles pyramids of equal height with the cone, and doing this repeatedly,",
              highlighted: PYR_N },
            { text: "we shall leave some segments of the cone which are less than the solid {X|Xf}.",
              highlighted: CONE_EN.concat(XBOX),
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.1" }] },
            { text: "Let such be left, and let them be the segments on {HP}, {PE}, {EQ}, {QF}, {FR}, {RG}, {GS}, and {SH}.",
              highlighted: CHORDS },
            { text: "Therefore the remainder, the pyramid with the polygonal base {HPEQFRGS} and the same height as that of the cone,",
              highlighted: PYR_N },
            { text: "is greater than the solid {O|Of}.",
              highlighted: PYR_N.concat(OBOX) },
            { text: "Now inscribe in the circle {ABCD|circABCD} the polygon {DTAUBVCW}",
              visible: POLY2,
              highlighted: ["DTAUBVCW"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "ABCD", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "T", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "U", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "V", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "W", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "AUBVCWDT", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "similar and similarly situated to the polygon {HPEQFRGS},",
              highlighted: ["DTAUBVCW","HPEQFRGS"] },
            { text: "and on it set up a pyramid of equal height with the cone {AL|coneAL}.",
              visible: PYL,
              highlighted: PYR_L,
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "lD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "lT", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "lA", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "lU", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "lB", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "lV", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "lC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "lW", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Since then the square on {AC} is to the square on {EG}",
              highlighted: ["AC","EG"] },
            { text: "as the polygon {DTAUBVCW} is to the polygon {HPEQFRGS},",
              highlighted: ["DTAUBVCW","HPEQFRGS"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "similar polygons inscribed in circles", ref: "XII.1" }] },
            { text: "while the square on {AC} is to the square on {EG} as the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH},",
              highlighted: ["AC","EG"].concat(CIRCS),
              justifications: [{ claim: "circles as the squares on their diameters", ref: "XII.2" }] },
            { text: "therefore the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as the polygon {DTAUBVCW} is to the polygon {HPEQFRGS}.",
              highlighted: CIRCS.concat(["DTAUBVCW","HPEQFRGS"]) },
            // Joyce's slip, left literal: "the solid 0" (for O).
            { text: "But the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as the cone {AL|coneAL} is to the solid 0,",
              highlighted: CIRCS.concat(["coneAL"]).concat(OBOX) },
            { text: "and the polygon {DTAUBVCW} is to the polygon {HPEQFRGS}",
              highlighted: ["DTAUBVCW","HPEQFRGS"] },
            { text: "as the pyramid with the polygonal base {DTAUBVCW} and the vertex {L}",
              highlighted: PYR_L },
            { text: "is to the pyramid with the polygonal base {HPEQFRGS} and the vertex {N}.",
              highlighted: PYR_N,
              justifications: [{ claim: "pyramids of the same height as their bases", ref: "XII.6" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the cone {AL|coneAL} is to the solid {O|Of}",
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(OBOX) },
            { text: "as the pyramid with the polygonal base {DTAUBVCW} and vertex {L}",
              highlighted: PYR_L },
            { text: "is to the pyramid with the polygonal base {HPEQFRGS} and vertex {N}.",
              highlighted: PYR_N,
              justifications: [{ claim: "ratios the same with the same ratio", ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, alternately the cone {AL|coneAL} is to the pyramid in it",
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(PYR_L) },
            { text: "as the solid {O|Of} is to the pyramid in the cone {EN|coneEN}.",
              highlighted: OBOX.concat(PYR_N),
              justifications: [{ claim: "alternately", ref: "V.16" }] },
            { text: "But the cone {AL|coneAL} is greater than the pyramid in it,",
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(PYR_L) },
            { text: "therefore the solid {O|Of} is also greater than the pyramid in the cone {EN|coneEN}.",
              highlighted: OBOX.concat(PYR_N) },
            { text: "But it is also less, which is absurd.",
              highlighted: OBOX.concat(PYR_N) },
            // Case 1 refuted: the construction and the solids are withdrawn.
            { text: "Therefore the cone {AL|coneAL} is not to any solid less than the cone {EN|coneEN}",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(CONE_EN) },
            { text: "as the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH}.",
              highlighted: CIRCS },
            { text: "Similarly we can prove that neither is the cone {EN|coneEN} to any solid less than the cone {AL|coneAL}",
              highlighted: CONE_EN.concat(CONE_AL) },
            { text: "as the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} is to the circle {ABCD|circABCD}.",
              highlighted: CIRCS },
            { text: "I say next that neither is the cone {AL|coneAL} to any solid greater than the cone {EN|coneEN}",
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(CONE_EN) },
            { text: "as the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH}.",
              highlighted: CIRCS },
            { text: "For, if possible, let it be in that ratio to a greater solid {O|Of}.",
              visible: SO,
              highlighted: OBOX },
            { text: "Therefore, inversely the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} is to the circle {ABCD|circABCD} as the solid {O|Of} is to the cone {AL|coneAL}.",
              highlighted: CIRCS.concat(OBOX).concat(["coneAL"]) },
            { text: "But the solid {O|Of} is to the cone {AL|coneAL} as the cone {EN|coneEN} to some solid less than the cone {AL|coneAL},",
              highlighted: OBOX.concat(CONE_AL).concat(CONE_EN) },
            { text: "therefore the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} is to the circle {ABCD|circABCD}",
              highlighted: CIRCS },
            { text: "as the cone {EN|coneEN} is to some solid less than the cone {AL|coneAL}, which was proved impossible.",
              highlighted: CONE_EN.concat(CONE_AL) },
            // Case 2 refuted: O is withdrawn again.
            { text: "Therefore the cone {AL|coneAL} is not to any solid greater than the cone {EN|coneEN}",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(CONE_EN) },
            { text: "as the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH}.",
              highlighted: CIRCS },
            { text: "But it was proved that neither is it in this ratio to a less solid,",
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(CONE_EN) },
            { text: "therefore the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as the cone {AL|coneAL} is to the cone {EN|coneEN}.",
              highlighted: CIRCS.concat(["coneAL","coneEN"]) },
            { text: "But the cone is to the cone as the cylinder is to the cylinder, for each is triple each.",
              highlighted: ["coneAL","coneEN"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "a cone is a third of its cylinder", ref: "XII.10" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as are the cylinders on them of equal height.",
              highlighted: CIRCS.concat(["KL","MN"]) },
            { text: "Therefore, cones and cylinders of the same height are to one another as their bases.",
              visible: REST,
              highlighted: CONE_AL.concat(CONE_EN),
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XII.11") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "IV.6":   "/elements/books/bookIV/propositions/propIV6/",
        "V.11":   "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV11/",
        "V.16":   "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV16/",
        "X.1":    "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX1/",
        "XII.1":  "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII1/",
        "XII.2":  "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII2/",
        "XII.6":  "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII6/",
        "XII.10": "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII10/"
    });
</script>
</center>

For, if not, then the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as the cone {AL|coneAL} is either to some solid less than the cone {EN|coneEN} or to a greater.

First, let it be in that ratio to a less solid {O|Of}, and let the solid {X|Xf} be equal to that by which the solid {O|Of} is less than the cone {EN|coneEN}. Therefore the cone {EN|coneEN} equals the sum of the solids {O|Of} and {X|Xf}.

Inscribe the square {EFGH|sqEFGH} in the circle {EFGH|circEFGH}. Therefore the square is greater than the half of the circle. [!just IV.6]

Set up from the square {EFGH|sqEFGH} a pyramid of equal height with the cone. Therefore the pyramid so set up is greater than the half of the cone, for if we circumscribe a square about the circle, and set up from it a pyramid of equal height with the cone, then the inscribed pyramid is half of the circumscribed pyramid, for they are to one another as their bases, while the cone is less than the circumscribed pyramid. [!just XII.6]

Bisect the circumferences {EF|arcEF}, {FG|arcFG}, {GH|arcGH}, and {HE|arcHE} at the points {P}, {Q}, {R}, and {S}, and join {HP}, {PE}, {EQ}, {QF}, {FR}, {RG}, {GS}, and {SH}.

Therefore each of the triangles {HPE}, {EQF}, {FRG}, and {GSH} is greater than the half of that segment of the circle about it.

Set up on each of the triangles {HPE}, {EQF}, {FRG}, and {GSH} a pyramid of equal height with the cone. Therefore each of the pyramids so set up is also greater than the half of that segment of the cone about it.

Thus, bisecting the circumferences which are left, joining straight lines, setting up on each of the triangles pyramids of equal height with the cone, and doing this repeatedly, we shall leave some segments of the cone which are less than the solid {X|Xf}. [!just X.1]

Let such be left, and let them be the segments on {HP}, {PE}, {EQ}, {QF}, {FR}, {RG}, {GS}, and {SH}. Therefore the remainder, the pyramid with the polygonal base {HPEQFRGS} and the same height as that of the cone, is greater than the solid {O|Of}.

Now inscribe in the circle {ABCD|circABCD} the polygon {DTAUBVCW} similar and similarly situated to the polygon {HPEQFRGS}, and on it set up a pyramid of equal height with the cone {AL|coneAL}.

Since then the square on {AC} is to the square on {EG} as the polygon {DTAUBVCW} is to the polygon {HPEQFRGS}, while the square on {AC} is to the square on {EG} as the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH}, therefore the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as the polygon {DTAUBVCW} is to the polygon {HPEQFRGS}. [!just XII.1; XII.2]

But the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as the cone {AL|coneAL} is to the solid 0, and the polygon {DTAUBVCW} is to the polygon {HPEQFRGS} as the pyramid with the polygonal base {DTAUBVCW} and the vertex {L} is to the pyramid with the polygonal base {HPEQFRGS} and the vertex {N}. [!just XII.6]

Therefore the cone {AL|coneAL} is to the solid {O|Of} as the pyramid with the polygonal base {DTAUBVCW} and vertex {L} is to the pyramid with the polygonal base {HPEQFRGS} and vertex {N}. Therefore, alternately the cone {AL|coneAL} is to the pyramid in it as the solid {O|Of} is to the pyramid in the cone {EN|coneEN}. [!just V.11; V.16]

But the cone {AL|coneAL} is greater than the pyramid in it, therefore the solid {O|Of} is also greater than the pyramid in the cone {EN|coneEN}.

But it is also less, which is absurd.

Therefore the cone {AL|coneAL} is not to any solid less than the cone {EN|coneEN} as the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH}.

Similarly we can prove that neither is the cone {EN|coneEN} to any solid less than the cone {AL|coneAL} as the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} is to the circle {ABCD|circABCD}.

I say next that neither is the cone {AL|coneAL} to any solid greater than the cone {EN|coneEN} as the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH}.

For, if possible, let it be in that ratio to a greater solid {O|Of}. Therefore, inversely the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} is to the circle {ABCD|circABCD} as the solid {O|Of} is to the cone {AL|coneAL}.

But the solid {O|Of} is to the cone {AL|coneAL} as the cone {EN|coneEN} to some solid less than the cone {AL|coneAL}, therefore the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} is to the circle {ABCD|circABCD} as the cone {EN|coneEN} is to some solid less than the cone {AL|coneAL}, which was proved impossible.

Therefore the cone {AL|coneAL} is not to any solid greater than the cone {EN|coneEN} as the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH}.

But it was proved that neither is it in this ratio to a less solid, therefore the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as the cone {AL|coneAL} is to the cone {EN|coneEN}.

But the cone is to the cone as the cylinder is to the cylinder, for each is triple each. Therefore the circle {ABCD|circABCD} is to the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as are the cylinders on them of equal height. [!just XII.10]

Therefore, *cones and cylinders of the same height are to one another as their bases.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

#### Use of this proposition

This proposition is used in the proofs of @XII.13 and @XII.14 when the cylinders under question have the same height and equal bases, and in the proof of @XII.15 for cylinders of different heights.
